WEBVTT

00:13:29.829 --> 00:13:33.454
You are trying to win your case. That
means the other side is wrong.

00:13:33.787 --> 00:13:36.204
And so you've got to get them
to do all the rethinking,

00:13:36.204 --> 00:13:37.621
but you get to stand still.

00:13:38.537 --> 00:13:40.621
And when you're thinking
more like a politician,

00:13:40.787 --> 00:13:44.704
you're basically trying to cater to your
audience and campaign for their approval

00:13:44.704 --> 00:13:46.329
or get their likes or their votes.

00:13:46.829 --> 00:13:51.162
And so you may be doing a little bit of
flexing in the way that you present,

00:13:51.162 --> 00:13:54.246
but you're not rethinking your
underlying beliefs. Right.

00:13:54.246 --> 00:13:56.787
You're just you're just trying
to appease your constituents.

00:13:57.454 --> 00:14:00.912
And I think we spend way too much
time thinking in these modes.